    "created_at": "2026-07-09T10:19:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-09T10:19:43Z",
    "body": "> Well, it would mean reverting this change, right? If an HTTP 'error' can produce a usable module, then we'd want it cached.\r\n\r\nFor persistent errors that may contain some useful info, sure.\r\nBut not for transient errors (e.g. 50X HTTP status codes, server resets, network went offline) we won't.\r\n\r\nSo I think we'd want a \"no cache\" path (as defined in this PR), and then potentially carve out the persistent errors (e.g. 4XX)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
